WEBVTT

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:36.490
In a surprising move, Team Psykick
challenged us to a battle!

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:42.260
It turns out that they were the ones with the Beys emitting magnetic waves!

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.910
These tough enemies keep
appearing one after another!

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.460
We can't underestimate them!

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:54.050
If we want to win, the BBA team must master it no matter what!

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:57.970
Yes! What Max's mom developed for us!

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.160
Max!

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.870
Over here!

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.160
Hey, guys!

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.540
Hope you've been well!

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.510
Yeah.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.040
I see you're early, Rei.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.670
I just got here.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.800
Who's she?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.880
She's nobody.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.800
I'm Hiromi Tachibana.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.350
Pleased to meet you.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.930
Miss Hiromi, huh?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.120
I'm Max. Nice to meet'cha.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.690
I never would have thought that there'd be

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.650
a cute girl waiting here for me.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.110
What's his deal?

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.150
Don't worry about him.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.110
He calls every girl cute,
even the weird ones.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:02:59.700
Oh, I see...

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.370
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.280
No, that's not what I--

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.300
Oh, Max!

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.160
You seem to be doing well.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.540
Chairman Daitenji!

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.920
It's good to see you!

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.590
I apologize for making
you come out all this way.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.170
It's no problem!

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.090
I get to battle again
with the team, after all.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:20.860
Right?

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.430
Yeah! The BBA Team is back in business!

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.310
So let's show 'em what we can do!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.850
Reliable as always.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.370
Your battle with Team
Psykick will be in one week.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:38.380
Please train hard until then.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:42.040
Okay! Training camp at
my place until the battle!

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.210
--Yeah!
--Yeah!

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:46.580
Hey, you can stay home.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.660
Why?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.040
It's not like you're on the team.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.800
Mr. Gideon.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.010
How are things advancing here?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.190
Steadily, sir.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.800
I see.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.970
I get it.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:14.190
So the guys you two battled
also haven't shown up since...

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.100
Yeah.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.150
I tried looking for him,

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.860
I never would have imagined that
they'd have invisible Sacred Beasts...

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.240
Just who are they?

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.000
What's your problem, Hiromi?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.500
It's not my problem!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.340
All I've been hearing is invisible Sacred Beasts this and mysterious boys that!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.670
Don't we have more important
things to worry about?

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:47.270
Your battle with Team
Psykick is in a week!

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.390
We know that.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.210
Do you really?

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.430
The future of humanity is at stake here!

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.870
The future of humanity?

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:58.610
She's just ranting. Don't give her attention.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.570
Takao!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.530
But I'm right, aren't I?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.780
Stop, you two!

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:09.880
I am worried about the ones
with the invisible Sacred Beasts,

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.580
but Hiromi is right.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:15.060
Let's focus on our
match with Team Psykick.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:19.000
They seem to be connected with the
scientists gunning for our Sacred Beasts.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.090
We shouldn't underestimate them!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.970
I forgot!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.800
Talk about sudden...

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.010
I forgot about something very important.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.430
Very important?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.640
Max, do you have it?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.140
I brought it with me.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.060
What's this?

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:44.570
I got Max's mom to make this for us, using the data from our opponents.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:45.900
It's the MG Core.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.240
MG Core?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:54.330
These were manufactured by pressurizing ores found in the central South America.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.920
When this is inserted into a
Bey and spun at high speeds,

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:06.480
it begins to emit a
powerful magnetic field.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:11.010
This magnetic system
reduces air resistance.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.920
Master it, and your Bey will be
under your complete control!

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.770
It'll move just how you want it to.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.870
Free control over a Bey
with this little thing...

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:25.710
Judging from their movements, it's safe to
assume Team Psykick uses something similar.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:31.000
We need to master the MG
Core if we want to defeat them.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.700
We've got this!

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.660
It'll be a piece of cake!

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.870
Let's give it a test run, okay?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.050
Okay. All ready!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:51.260
Time to show off my
awesome Bey control skills.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:54.510
Go Shoot!

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.940
There it is!

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.400
So this is the magnet system?

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.670
Go, Dragoon!

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.910
Lightning-fast turn!

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.830
That's some lightning-fast turn...

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.860
Wasn't even close...

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.710
Shut up! I just messed up a little!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.790
I'm up next.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.550
What's that?

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.920
Is that a new Bey?

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.900
It's the Driger Vulcan.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:33.220
I brought Driger up to the next level.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.810
Go Shoot!

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.560
It's out!

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.560
Driger!

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:47.780
Hey now...

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.150
Wow, Driger Vulcan!

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.780
Stop! Come on, stop!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.510
I wonder what the problem is?

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:01.120
The Metal Flat Tip is amplifying
the magnetic forces.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.420
Is that why it can't stop?

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.170
Yes.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:08.960
But if he can control it, Driger
Vulcan's speed will double!

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.460
Double?!

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:10.970
If he can control it.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.090
--Driger!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.340
Darn it!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.390
Okay!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.720
You two are putting too much force into it.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.560
I'll show you how it's
done, so watch and learn.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.650
Time to show off!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.860
Go Shoot!

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.410
Go, Draciel!

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.490
Do a triple jump!

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.750
Look who's the got the worst
control after all that big talk!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:50.420
You sure showed us how it's done!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.340
Are these guys really world champions?

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.260
I'm up next.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.680
Let's go, Dranzer!

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.110
I think he's got it this time!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.660
Are they going to be okay?

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.120
Beats me.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.790
One and two... One and two...

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:33.920
One, two, three, four...

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.180
Good morning!

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.680
Good morning, Hiromi!

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.720
She's such a polite girl.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.180
Good morning...

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.780
Right... there was a technique to waking him up...

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.210
Too easy, grandpa!

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.600
Ow...

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.590
Oh, it's just Hiromi...

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.470
Don't "it's just Hiromi" me!

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.010
Rise and shine!

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.140
Get dressed because it's time to train!

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.230
What's all the fuss?

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.230
It's not even 6 a.m. yet...

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.110
So sleepy...

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.480
This is it!

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.410
"1: Straight Run,"

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.410
"2: Left Turn, 3: Right"...

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:43.740
The heck is this?

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:46.540
I whipped up this training regimen!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.500
--Training regimen?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.750
You're all trying way too hard.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.790
You can't just jump in
and expect to master it.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:57.510
You gotta start from
the basics with this stuff!

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.680
Don't just stare off into space!

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:02.930
C'mon! Let's get started!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.890
Listen up, Hiromi. What do you take us for, huh?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.930
We're the world champions.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.270
I'm not gonna do these practice
drills made for beginners.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.190
World champions?

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.030
You can't even control it.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.440
What?!

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:21.110
If you don't like it then try doing one of those lightning-fast turns.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.830
I don't have time for this.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.870
Let's get outta here.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.240
Stop!

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:28.750
What's with the attitude?

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.920
After all the work I put in for you!

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:34.420
Look, we've got our own
ways of doing things!

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.760
And Kyoujyu, hurry up
and put that thing down!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.170
What do you
think you're doing?!

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:41.470
What?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.300
Let go!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.800
You let go!

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.180
No, you!

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.810
What have you done?!

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:54.190
It's because you pulled too hard!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.440
Are you saying it's my fault?

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.690
I am!

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.190
No one asked you!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.820
It's your fault for
making this crap!

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.530
This is none of your business.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:07.330
Don't get ahead of yourself when
you've never even spun a Beyblade before!

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.540
You didn't have to put it like that.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:17.040
I thought that I could do something, too.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.670
So I tried my best to put this together...

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.720
Fine!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.700
Suit yourselves!

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:26.050
Hiromi...

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.850
Don't you think that was too far?

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:33.020
She looked pretty hurt.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.860
She'll be fine.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.320
Let's get practicing.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:13:04.350
Hiromi...

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:05.630
Hiromi!

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.800
Oh, Kyoujyu, do you need something?

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:11.220
Not "need", but...

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.640
Is practice going well?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.650
Yeah, sort of...

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.230
Good.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.320
See you tomorrow.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.150
Ah, Hiromi!

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.280
You know, right?

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:26.740
Takao didn't mean what he said.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.640
Kyoujyu!

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:33.000
What's the holdup? If you
don't hurry I'm gonna leave you...

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.410
behind...

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.920
I'm going on ahead.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.630
We'll be waiting, Hiromi!

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.340
Wait up, Takao!

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.010
Go Shoot!

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.230
Pretty good!

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:00.900
Dragoon! One last turn!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:10.030
Darn! I was so close, too!

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.830
Okay, I'm up next.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.250
Is there a problem?

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:22.040
No, I was just wondering
where Hiromi disappeared to.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.000
Uh...

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.300
Today isn't...

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:30.820
I see. She wasn't
here yesterday either,

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:33.180
so I hope she didn't get sick.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.180
No, she's fine!

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.480
She's in great shape! Yup!

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:40.730
That's good to hear.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:43.490
Kyoujyu!

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:45.380
Pay attention!

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.860
Sorry.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:57.290
We're almost there...
what are we missing?

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.870
We're better off than
we were at the start.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.090
We've still got three days left.
No need to panic yet.

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:04.710
We'll figure something out.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:08.420
Even if we can move a little faster,
what's the point if we can't battle?

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.880
You guys get it, right?

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.140
Well, yes, but...

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:14.850
What aren't we getting?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:44.540
One, two, three, four...

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.470
It's too early for this...

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.190
What's this?

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.150
What's up, Takao?

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.140
Kai... How did you...

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.600
Don't make fun of the basics.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:48.610
Takao...

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.860
The basics really are important!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.380
Listen...

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:04.210
I'm sorry for what I said earlier.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:07.040
We only have two
days until our match.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:11.390
We were wondering if you could
make another training regimen for us?

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:13.840
Yeah! A great one!

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:18.300
But I've never
spun a Bey before...

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:21.520
That's okay! I'll help too!

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:23.350
So please!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.850
We're counting on you.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.730
Guess I don't have a choice.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:33.290
I'm not gonna be nice
so you better be ready!

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:36.070
--Yes! Don't hold back!
--Yes! Don't hold back!

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:40.870
Hey, there's no lunch
break anywhere in here!

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.330
If you don't master the MG Core,

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.870
There'll be no lunch for you!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.080
Darn straight!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.380
What? What'd you say?!

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.430
Good going, Kai! Keep it up!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.220
Go Shoot!

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.270
His turn is too wide.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.140
Takao! Do a tigher turn! Tighter!

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.850
Darn!

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:14.740
You suck! What the
heck are you doing?!

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:17.280
What?!

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:20.030
I lost my focus because
you keep yapping at me!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.370
So it's my fault?

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:23.490
It is! Who else's would it be?!

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:24.870
I'm gonna--

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.250
Fool!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:31.000
What was that for?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.300
I won't allow anyone
to bully Hiromi.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.420
That's not fair...

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:48.390
Go Shoot!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.460
Time for the finishing touch.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.050
Don't lose focus because
you're in battle now.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:20.090
Fight with what you're learned.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:21.130
Got it?

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.800
Hard at work I see.

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:24.930
Chairman Daitenji!

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:28.230
Today's the day. Do your best.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.770
Here we go.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.770
Three! Two! One!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:36.020
Go Shoot!

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:49.870
There it is!

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:00.560
Incredible...

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.880
The magnetic fields are
repelling each other!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.740
Go Dragoon!

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:08.100
Don't lose to him, Dranzer!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.610
The bus is here!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.610
Alright! Time to go!

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:25.490
We're gonna go wild on 'em!

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:26.830
--Yeah!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.450
All aboard!

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.460
The time has come.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.290
Grandpa...

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.500
I'll be rootin' for you.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.710
Show 'em what you're made of.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:37.630
Yes!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.340
I'm off!

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:02.900
We were supposed to
head to the arena,

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:05.950
but instead we're greeted to a
forest filled to the brim with traps!

00:23:05.950 --> 00:23:09.030
Dangers and mysterious enemies
are coming out of the woodwork!

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:11.530
It's like a rollercoaster! Huh?

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:13.910
Go on ahead, grandpa
will be waiting for you?

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:17.000
That's an amusement park!
That's not what I meant!

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:20.420
Anyway, you won't want to miss next week's episode, Chairman Daitenji!
